get should be met by:\n\n1. Linear dimension search range [n-300, n+300] with checkpoints\n2. Quantum-inspired crossover rate deterministic re-initialization (10%)\n3. Apex-edge crossover budget balancing (800 vs 400)\n4. Periodic evaluation with rescoring (mixed first-principle and surrogate)\n5. Condenser states discipline\n\nTrack historical minima (stored in best_condenser) and\u7981\u533a\u3078\n\nFinally, within the program, evaluate with:\n\nevaluate_sequence = function to be called for final confirmation\n\nBut the evolutionary search should be faster due to dimension-aware advantages and lower-dimensional components.\n\nThe previous program's overall score approach is:\n\nTarget: <1.5027 to be achieved\n\nWe will improve by adding quantum-inspired dimension awareness and explicit restart mechanism.\n\nImplementation complexity:\n\n- Uses numpy extensively for vector computations\n- Relies on simplex projection at base\n- Keeps log during evolution for checkpoint reporting\n- Time estimates must be offline-safe\n\nGet detailed benchmarking from simulation or offline runs for confidence intervals.\n\nStart_time = time.time()\n\nThe program must be resistant to local optima (over 10 restarts) but aggressively follow simplex-like principles.\n\nReturns the sequence list after each evolution step if budget allows, else falls back to initial.\n\nIf time runs out early (before 50 steps) -> return best_candidate\n\nElse -> perform full quantum-inspired search and dimensions-perturbation\n\nPeriodic restarts set adaptive momentum levels.\n\nLet\u2019s code accordingly.",
